#. Tag: title
#: variables.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working With Variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: variables.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the inspector dialog is not showing use the <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show inspectors</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> menu item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: variables.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Local and global variables are show in a tab on the inspector dialog. The "
"following example shows a XSLT code segment that declares a global and a "
"local variable"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: variables.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;xsl:variable name=\"globalvariable\" select=\"'foo'\"/&gt;\n"
"\n"
"    &lt;xsl:template match=\"/\"/&gt;\n"
"        &lt;xsl:param name=\"localvariable\" select=\"'bar'\"/&gt;\n"
"    &lt;/xsl:template match=\"/\"/&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: variables.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking with with mouse on a variable in the list will cause summary "
"information to be displayed in the bottom of the dialog. If a variable has a "
"select expression, for example"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: variables.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;xsl:variable name=\"changeable\" select=\"'oldValue'\" /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: variables.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"then a new XPath can be chosen by entering a new value for "
"<guilabel>Variable expression</guilabel> then clicking the <guibutton>Set "
"expression</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: variables.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Variables tab"
msgstr ""

